/// DynamicSupervisor for the optional `ExduraHttpServer` child.
///
/// A single-child pool, always present in `ExduraSupervisor`'s static
/// tree — even when HTTP isn't configured, it just stays childless. The
/// dynamic-supervisor route (rather than a static `SupervisionSpec` on
/// `ExduraSupervisor` itself) exists because the HTTP server's port and
/// workflow registry are runtime config from `ExduraWorker start: config`,
/// not something `ExduraSupervisor class children` (a parameterless class
/// method, evaluated once at supervisor init) can see.
///
/// `startChild: args` bakes those args into the OTP child spec, so a crash
/// restarts `ExduraHttpServer` with the exact same port/engine/store it
/// was started with (BT-3365) — the listener comes back up on its own,
/// same as every other child in the tree, instead of silently staying
/// down.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// httpSup := (sup which: ExduraHttpServerSupervisor) unwrap
/// http := httpSup startChild: #{
///   #port => 4100, #engine => engine, #store => store, #workflowClasses => #(OrderWorkflow)
/// }
/// ```
///
/// @see ExduraHttpServer (the supervised child)
DynamicSupervisor(ExduraHttpServer) subclass: ExduraHttpServerSupervisor
  class childClass => ExduraHttpServer
